=== dit deletes between the tags
ref:    motion.txt *it*
quote:  "\"inner tag block\", select [count] tag blocks"
given:  <b>fo|o</b>
keys:   dit
expect: <b>|</b>
regs:   "" = "foo"
undo:   <b>|foo</b>

=== dat deletes the tags too
ref:    motion.txt *at*
quote:  "including the \"<aaa>\" and \"</aaa>\"."
given:  x <b>fo|o</b> y
keys:   dat
expect: x | y
regs:   "" = "<b>foo</b>"

=== dit with the cursor on the opening tag
ref:    motion.txt *tag-blocks*
quote:  The normal method is to select a <tag> until the matching </tag>.
given:  <|b>foo</b>
keys:   dit
expect: <b>|</b>
regs:   "" = "foo"

=== dit with the cursor on the closing tag
ref:    motion.txt *tag-blocks*
quote:  The normal method is to select a <tag> until the matching </tag>.
given:  <b>foo</|b>
keys:   dit
expect: <b>|</b>
regs:   "" = "foo"

=== dit picks the innermost tag block
ref:    motion.txt *it*
quote:  "from the [count]'th unmatched \"<aaa>\" backwards to the matching \"</aaa>\""
given:  <a><b>|x</b></a>
keys:   dit
expect: <a><b>|</b></a>
regs:   "" = "x"

=== d2it deletes inside the second enclosing tag block
ref:    motion.txt *it*
quote:  select [count] tag blocks
given:  <a>1<b>|x</b>2</a>
keys:   d2it
expect: <a>|</a>
regs:   "" = "1<b>x</b>2"

=== d2at deletes the second enclosing tag block
ref:    motion.txt *at*
quote:  select [count] tag blocks
given:  z<a>1<b>|x</b>2</a>z
keys:   d2at
expect: z|z
regs:   "" = "<a>1<b>x</b>2</a>"

=== dat on a tag nested between text keeps the outer block
ref:    motion.txt *at*
quote:  "including the \"<aaa>\" and \"</aaa>\"."
given:  <a>1<b>|x</b>2</a>
keys:   dat
expect: <a>1|2</a>
regs:   "" = "<b>x</b>"

=== dit matches tags ignoring case
ref:    motion.txt *tag-blocks*
quote:  Case is ignored, also for XML where case does matter.
given:  <B>fo|o</b>
keys:   dit
expect: <B>|</b>
regs:   "" = "foo"

=== dit skips self-closing tags
ref:    motion.txt *tag-blocks*
quote:  "\"<aaa/>\" items are skipped."
given:  <p>a<br/>|b</p>
keys:   dit
expect: <p>|</p>
regs:   "" = "a<br/>b"

=== dit tolerates a tag with attributes
ref:    motion.txt *tag-blocks*
quote:  The normal method is to select a <tag> until the matching </tag>.
given:  <a href="x">l|ink</a>
keys:   dit
expect: <a href="x">|</a>
regs:   "" = "link"

=== dit over several lines
ref:    motion.txt *it*
quote:  excluding the "<aaa>" and "</aaa>".
given:
  <div>
    |x
  </div>
keys:   dit
expect:
  <div>|</div>
regs:   "" = "\n  x\n"

=== dit on an empty tag block deletes nothing
ref:    motion.txt *tag-blocks*
quote:  Also, "it" used on a tag block with no contents will select the leading tag.
given:  x <b>|</b> y
keys:   dit
expect: x <b>|</b> y
regs:   "" = (unset)

=== dit with no tags does nothing
ref:    motion.txt *it*
quote:  "\"inner tag block\", select [count] tag blocks"
given:  foo |bar
keys:   dit
expect: foo |bar
regs:   "" = (unset)

=== cit replaces the tag contents
ref:    motion.txt *it*
quote:  excluding the "<aaa>" and "</aaa>".
given:  <i>o|ld</i>
keys:   citnew<Esc>
expect: <i>ne|w</i>
regs:   "" = "old"
